        "note": "Uses canonical IsNowhereDense, IsMeagre, residual filters, countable intersections, actual product topology and open coordinate projections. Mathlib BaireMeasurableSet is the property of Baire (open modulo meagre), not the separate Baire sigma-algebra generated by continuous functions; its residualEq_isOpen bridge and Baire category lemmas are credited. No equivalent section theorem was located in bounded pinned-library audit. The substantive new bridge constructs a countable family of projected dense open sets and assembles generic-section implications. Exact BaireMeasurableSet definition: https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/065356127b1dc0016f66b7283ce0ce2c4055aa55/Mathlib/Topology/Baire/BaireMeasurable.lean#L91-L92 . The proved open-set equivalence is at lines182–184 in that same pinned file. MATERIAL-DEFINITIONS.md retains literal source excerpts, the Borel/residual dependency chain, hashes and attribution; verification/material-imported-definitions.json binds the audited evidence. ChallengeTests and SemanticTests independently prove the open symmetric-difference/meagre characterization and apply it to both converse contracts; no theorem meaning or hypothesis changes.",
